-    rises away from the plane) bound a sliver thinner than the mesh can carry.  Their vertices are snapped onto the
-    plane, so the flat-triangle drop removes them and the cap closes the solid there.  Snapping only some vertices of
-    such a patch (the plain near-plane snap) pinches the sheet onto the cap along an interior edge, an edge with four
-    triangles (census 2026-09-04, sheet tangent to the cut plane beside a face edge).  Iterated: a flattened patch can
